  "limitations": [
    "Generalized accounting is a pure proposal calculator. Manifest, parent/head, identity, D2 attempt count, journal and closure must be independently verified and reread under transaction locks before future ingestion. Java records do not authenticate any proof.",
    "No SQL V24 or multicheckpoint/multi-account route, CAS/readset integration or new Compose campaign has been implemented. Existing V23 keeps its one-checkpoint/two-step/one-account rejection guards.",
    "Local Python verifiers are separate from the Java HTTPS verifier. No worker object import, artifact publication protocol, signed ingestion or ACCEPTANCE_PASS bridge is implemented.",
    "File observation requires independently stopped writers; this does not provide an atomic tree snapshot against concurrent mutation or future writes.",
    "Git only supports verifier-owned, newly initialized bare fixture stores, bounded regular blobs and approved bases. No hooks, filters, LFS, symlinks, submodules or arbitrary repository import.",
    "Restoration checks local file state only. APPLIED receipts and consumed units remain authoritative; no external compensation or UNKNOWN/contradiction resolution is introduced.",
    "Real provider costs, nonzero restart costs and variable per-attempt metering are excluded under A14. Existing 70/20/10, dependencies, blocking-path priority, reservation and fencing behavior is preserved, not newly proved by the pure calculator.",
    "Historical JUnit targets remain distinct; the 81 D4 tests are components and historical checkpoint/polling SQL tests, not 81 generalized SQL/Compose tests.",
    "No real provider/credential, migration promotion, deployment or D4 closure."
